=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: pc1
diagnosis_text:
The fault is a service outage on pc1, the sole host on the Server Room (lan_servers, 1.0.0.0/8) segment. Apache2 is installed on pc1 and its web root is populated with content (a 10 KB index.html in /var/www/html), but the daemon is not running — `service apache2 status` confirms "apache2 is not running." Nothing is listening on any TCP/UDP port; every inbound connection attempt receives an immediate "Connection refused" at the kernel level. The SSH/SFTP server is similarly absent.

The L3 infrastructure is fully healthy: cs_lab1 (192.168.2.3) pings pc1 (1.0.0.5) with 0% loss through the three-hop RIP-routed path (router0 → router1 → router2), and all routers carry symmetric routes for both 192.168.2.0/24 and 1.0.0.0/8. No ACL or nftables rule on pc1 blocks any protocol. Traffic control is clean on all 43 interfaces.

The direct cause is pc1's startup script: it configures the network interface and default route but contains no service-start command for Apache or SSH. A comment in the script reads `"servers DNS/FTP/WEB excluded per spec"`, which is evidence that the service-start lines were removed (or never added in the injected version of the script). Because Kathara runs startup scripts at container boot, Apache never started. All CS lab users hit the same wall simultaneously — Connection refused on port 80 — because the server has no listener to accept any of their connections.

Root cause: Apache2 (web/file server) was not started on pc1 because its startup script was stripped of service-launch commands, leaving the Server Room host with no application services running.

Fix: Add `service apache2 start` (and `service ssh start` if SFTP access is also required) to pc1's startup script, then restart the pc1 container so the corrected script executes.
=== END ===